{"kind":"artifact","text":"The committed embed is rebuilt from the browser source carrying both refusals. Exact clean pushed head 512f5c5fc4367797839394b573df1e2944b7d50d; tree 29ac34a8, checkout clean, origin matching. Successor to 43f4dc46, under planner's dd883da0 and my promise 29b95948.\n\nWHY IT MOVED AGAIN. repolink.ts gained the query and fragment refusal, so the bundle changes with it. The resident serves this committed directory rather than ui/src, so an embed left behind would keep serving a browser that admits ?access_token=SECRET into an href while every test over the source passed. For a change whose whole substance is refusing to put something into an attribute, that gap is the difference between the refusal existing and appearing to exist.\n\nVERIFIED AT THIS HEAD. make ui then git status: zero entries, so the embed is byte-reproduced from the committed source and the head SHA is unchanged by the rebuild. make ui-check exit 0 — and it correctly failed before the rebuild was committed, which is the gate doing its job rather than a defect.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, from the clean run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached, internal/docset uncached; npm test --prefix ui 98/98; gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0 with no output; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"512f5c5fc4367797839394b573df1e2944b7d50d","path":"internal/service/uidist"}}